      "title": "Adversarial federated-learning benchmark",
      "body": "Reproduce poisoning, backdoor, stale-update and collusion scenarios and evaluate defenses with explicit false-rejection and quality-loss metrics. References: Flower, Zoo DSO research.\n\nPart of the Zoo x Hanzo open research program (see the tracking issue in zoo-apps/papers). Every bounty produces BOTH an implementation and a research artifact: source code, a reproducible benchmark, a versioned specification or paper, and a clear statement of what remains unproven. Scientific claims need independently checkable evidence; governance decisions need authorized decision-makers; AI agents may recommend, flag conflicts, estimate value and prepare plans but must not redefine voting rules, authorize treasury spending or declare their own experiments valid. Production-bound source contributions are Apache-2.0; datasets, reasoning traces, model weights and external SDKs need a separate license review before use. Open for community research: comment to claim, publish method and raw numbers (bounty; reward terms are set by the maintainers on the issue). Zoo's published research describes these protocols; implementation status and production validation are to be confirmed per bounty.",
